00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:48.290
Our AI analysis is learning from volume confirmation patterns and adjusting position sizing accordingly.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:55.550
Imagine you bought GE Healthcare last night after seeing the pre-market plus 10% move on the earnings beat.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:01.210
Your order filled at the open but the actual price path between the headline and your fill,

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:08.470
dependent on how many shares were already queued at the ask and whether market makers widen spreads in the first minutes of trading.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:16.410
The mechanism works through order imbalance when positive news hits, buy orders pile up faster than sellers can supply shares.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:22.970
Pushing the bid ask spread from a few cents to 20-30 cents and creating slippage for late entrance.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:31.970
Professionals always check the level 2 book and recent volume profile before the open to gauge whether the move has real participation or is thin.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:38.830
The biggest mistake with earnings reactions is assuming the headline percentage move will hold through the first hour.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:47.710
Instead, always wait for the first 15-minute candle to close and confirm volume above the 20-day average before adding to the position.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:54.650
Vertives simultaneous 13% pre-market drop on its earnings miss illustrates the opposite imbalance,

00:11:55.150 --> 00:12:00.730
where sell orders overwhelm bids and spreads can widen even further in the opposite direction.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:12.190
A second concrete example appears in how BMW's voluntary severance announcement for thousands of German workers expected to cover most of the planned 8,000 global cuts.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:17.590
May create a similar pre-market reaction window once regular session volume arrives.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:27.670
The pro tip is to cross-reference the earnings headline against the company's own guidance language rather than relying solely on the percentage move printed by the headline service.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:35.570
This prevents entering positions where the market has already priced in the full extent of the beat or miss within the first 5 minutes.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:47.110
Before we wrap, pull up the options chain for any stock you already own in a TFSA and calculate the annualized yield on the 30-day out of the money covered call.

